🚽 Test case: round-22 review finding #1 -- handle_function_call() (ast.c)
🚽 boxed a return value by switching on its base VarType FIRST, with
🚽 pointer-boxing special-cased only inside the VAR_INT/VAR_ENUM cases.
🚽 A user-defined function returning `skibidi *` (any base type at all,
🚽 pointer_level > 0) fell into VAR_VOID's own "structurally unreachable"
🚽 case instead, returning NULL despite genuinely having a value --
🚽 `identity_ptr(p)` handing its caller a null pointer regardless of
🚽 what `p` actually pointed at. Fixed by checking pointer_level BEFORE
🚽 the base-type switch, dominant over it, matching how the native-call
🚽 marshaller (ast_expr_to_stdrot_value(), stdrot.c) already treats
🚽 pointer-ness. Confirmed via a temporary A/B test (git stash to the
🚽 pre-fix commit) that `q` silently ended up null.
skibidi *identity_ptr(skibidi *p) {
    bussin p;
}

skibidi main {
    skibidi *p = test_ptr_source();
    skibidi *q = identity_ptr(p);

    edgy (q != 0) {
        yapping("alive");
    }

    bussin 0;
}
